course: dictionary
lesson: 10997
title: Many meanings, one word
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: One word can have several meanings. The clues in the sentence tell you which meaning the writer wants. «Before washing machines, people scrubbed clothes on a washboard.» The clue is scrubbed clothes, so a washboard is something you wash clothes on.
explain: Now read a different sentence: «The skiffle band had a washboard player who scraped out a fast rhythm.» The clues are band and rhythm, so here a washboard is a musical instrument. Ask yourself: which meaning fits this sentence?
explain: Check your choice by swapping the meaning into the sentence. If "a board for scrubbing" does not fit a band, try "an instrument". If the new meaning makes sense, you have found the right one.
fact: A washboard is a board with ridges on it, once used for scrubbing clothes by hand.
fact: Skiffle and folk music players use a washboard as an instrument, scraping it to make a rhythm.
fact: Informal: «washboard stomach» means very flat, strong stomach muscles.
fact: In North America, a bumpy dirt road with ridges is called a washboard road.
fact: In The Wind in the Willows, Toad escapes prison dressed as a washerwoman, and later he is no good at washing clothes on a barge.
exercise: «Before washing machines, people scrubbed clothes on a washboard.» What is a washboard in this sentence? | A bumpy road | A kind of musical drum | *A board with ridges for scrubbing clothes | A flat stomach with strong muscles
exercise: «The skiffle band had a washboard player who scraped out a fast rhythm.» In this sentence, what is a washboard? | A bumpy dirt road | A very flat stomach | *A musical instrument played by scraping | A board for ironing shirts
exercise: Which informal phrase describes very flat, strong stomach muscles? | Skiffle band | *Washboard stomach | Mangle roller | Washboard road
test: «The dusty road was full of ridges, like a washboard.» What does washboard mean here? | A flat stomach | Something clean and shiny | *A bumpy road with ridges | A musical instrument played loudly
test: Why can one word have several meanings? | Dictionaries are often wrong | *The clues in the sentence show which meaning fits | Only music words have more than one meaning | Every word means only one thing
exam: Look at «Toad had to wash clothes on a barge and was no good at it.» What is a washboard most likely to be in a story about washing? | Something to play music on | A kind of road | *Something to scrub clothes on | A flat stomach
